# The Swedish Club as text: the system's meanings, and the built-in scenarios written with them.
#
# These are the scenarios `sim` and Bridge Workbench ship: read before any folder of yours, shown read only in the
# scenario editor. Each was a compiled scenario of the same name (`scenarios.odin`), and
# `test_the_text_swedish_club_is_the_compiled_one` still holds every one to it deal for deal (and its label, former
# name, description, system and tags).
#
# YOUR OWN VERSION of the system extends this one and overrides only the meanings you play differently:
#
#     system ours extends swedish-club "WSC as we play it"
#       meaning nt-opening: hcp in 15..17 and nt-shape
#
# A meaning may name a compiled predicate (`is_3n_opener`) where the language cannot say the thing itself. The
# scenarios with no system (hand types, partnership totals, the opponents' auctions) cannot use the system's
# meanings, so they name the predicates directly.

system swedish-club "the Swedish Club played here: 1NT 16-18, a 1M of 11-15, 2C a club one-suiter"
  # This system's notrump shape: 4333, 4432 or 5332 with the five in ANY suit (`deal`'s 5CM_nt). The language's
  # `balanced` never includes a five-card major, so the shapes are named.
  meaning nt-shape: shape(any 4333, any 4432, any 5332)
  # Balanced or semi-balanced (every suit two to six cards, no major longer than five): what "not flat" excludes.
  meaning flattish: balanced or semibalanced
  # The two-suited shapes: 5-5, 6-4, 6-5, 7-4 and 7-5; then those with ten cards in the two longest suits (6-4 and
  # 7-3), with eleven or more (6-5, 6-6, 7-4, 7-5, 8-4), and the lopsided ones (6-4 up to 8-4, not 5-5).
  meaning two-suiter: shape(any 5521, any 5530, any 6421, any 6430, any 6520, any 6511, any 7411, any 7420, any 7510)
  meaning two-suiter-10: shape(any 6421, any 6430, any 7321, any 7330)
  meaning two-suiter-11: shape(any 6520, any 6511, any 6610, any 7411, any 7420, any 7510, any 8410)
  meaning two-suiter-lopsided: shape(any 6421, any 6430, any 6520, any 6511, any 7411, any 7420, any 7510, any 8410)
  meaning nt-opening: hcp in 16..18 and nt-shape
  meaning 2nt-opening: hcp in 19..20 and nt-shape
  # 1C: the 13-15 notrump hand, or a strong hand (21+, or 16-20 that is not flat).
  meaning weak-1c: hcp in 13..15 and nt-shape
  meaning strong-1c: hcp >= 21 or hcp >= 16 and not flattish
  meaning 1c-opening: weak-1c or strong-1c
  # A limited major: 11-15 with a five-card major, not the 13-15 notrump hand (that opens 1C), not a hand
  # with a longer minor, not a gambling 3NT. The light one is the same at 9-11.
  meaning major-opening: hcp in 11..15 and (spades >= 5 or hearts >= 5) and not weak-1c and not longer-minor and not is_3n_opener
  meaning light-major-opening: hcp in 9..11 and (spades >= 5 or hearts >= 5) and not weak-1c and not longer-minor and not is_3n_opener
  meaning longer-minor: clubs > spades and clubs > hearts or diamonds > spades and diamonds > hearts
  # Support for the major North opened, of 3 or 4 cards: a deal line's meaning, naming both hands.
  meaning major-support-3: north(spades >= 5) and south(spades >= 3) or north(hearts >= 5) and south(hearts >= 3)
  meaning major-support-4: north(spades >= 5) and south(spades >= 4) or north(hearts >= 5) and south(hearts >= 4)
  # 1D: an unbalanced 11-15 with diamonds the longest suit (four or more) that is not a 2C or 2D hand - or a
  # balanced 11-13 that is not a major opening.
  meaning 1d-unbal: not flattish and hcp in 11..15 and not 2c-opening and not 2d-intermediate and diamonds >= 4 and diamonds > spades and diamonds > hearts
  meaning 1d-opening: 1d-unbal or not major-opening and hcp in 11..13 and nt-shape
  # 2C: six or more clubs, 11-15 (or exactly 10 with seven), and no other suit of six.
  meaning 2c-opening: hcp <= 15 and spades <= 5 and hearts <= 5 and diamonds <= 5 and ((clubs >= 6 and hcp >= 11) or (clubs = 7 and hcp = 10))
  # Precision 2D: 4-4-1-4 with 12-16, or 4-4-0-5 / 4-3-1-5 / 3-4-1-5 with 11-15.
  meaning 2d-precision: spades = 4 and hearts = 4 and diamonds = 1 and clubs = 4 and hcp in 12..16 or clubs = 5 and (spades = 4 and hearts = 4 and diamonds = 0 or spades = 4 and hearts = 3 and diamonds = 1 or spades = 3 and hearts = 4 and diamonds = 1) and hcp in 11..15
  # The intermediate 2D: six or more diamonds, the longest suit, no five-card major, 9-15 - a 9 or 10 needs a
  # second suit.
  meaning 2d-intermediate: hcp in 9..15 and diamonds >= 6 and diamonds >= clubs and hearts <= 4 and spades <= 4 and (hcp >= 11 or hcp = 10 and (two-suiter-10 or two-suiter-11) or hcp = 9 and two-suiter-11)
  meaning weak-two: is_weak2_major
  meaning gambling-3nt: is_3n_opener


scenario 1c "North opens 1C (any strength)"
  label: 1♣
  formerly: 1c-any
  system: swedish-club
  north: 1c-opening


scenario 1c-1n "1C opener; South makes any 1NT response"
  label: 1♣ – 1NT
